00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:17.060
I do remember that Hal was digging in the yard.

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:19.060
What time were you digging, Hal?

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:21.520
- All day, it was my Hal dig all day day.

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:25.030
- I was juggling acorns.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:28.130
Five acorns was a world record for me.

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:30.000
And I certainly didn't do it all day.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.400
Sweet! But what time did you set your world record?

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:37.430
Daisy, I'm a wild mouse. I have no concept of time.

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:43.200
Daisy, you were taking pictures all day. Maybe we can find some clues there.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:47.040
Oh, great idea! Inspiration was flowing like the sunlight.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.930
Oh, oh my, oh, oh, you should see these nature pictorials.

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.170
Oh, here's one I took very early in the morning.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:56.570
See how the shadows play off the flowers? It's all so, so nature-y.

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:58.570
Whoa! Oh, what's this?

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:00.000
Hey, look, you guys!

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.020
I can't see it from all the way up here.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.840
I took this picture yesterday.

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:08.760
Hey, that's my doghouse.

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:09.760
I live there.

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:11.760
Why are we looking at Hal's doghouse, Daze?

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:12.760
Look here.

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:14.770
That's the doghouse.

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:15.770
Hey, that's me.

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:17.770
And Norman the squirrel.

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:18.770
Hey, look at that.

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:21.770
The shadow is on the wrong side of Hal's doghouse.

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:23.660
What do you mean it's on the wrong side?

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.670
There's nothing wrong with my doghouse or its shadow.

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:28.670
No, no, no.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.000
Hal, look at your doghouse.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.900
The shadow now is in a different place than in Daisy's picture.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:36.250
Oh, yeah, well, I'll have to get that fixed.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:38.770
There's nothing to fix, Hal.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:41.630
The shadow's here because it's morning now.

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:44.630
In the picture, the shadow is on this side.

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:48.460
Oh, no! My doghouse moved!

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:51.410
No, Hal. Your doghouse didn't move.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:54.410
The position of the sun changed in the sky.

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:55.910
As the sun's position changed,

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:58.410
the position of your doghouse shadow changed, too.

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:00.000
Oh, no!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.400
What if Norman the squirrel was already here?

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:07.600
What if I already miss something unbelievably, incredibly, amazingly nature caddy?

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:11.120
You couldn't have missed it. You've been sitting in this tree all morning

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:13.760
and Daisy took the picture later in the day.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:19.040
We know that because the shadow on Hal's doghouse is moving in the direction of the shadow in my picture.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.090
It's getting closer and closer.

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:24.930
Fine. I'll just sit right here until the shadow on Hal's doghouse

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:29.730
matches the shadow in your picture, because that's when Norman will be back.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:33.420
Good idea. To make sure we don't miss the time,

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:36.720
let's mark the spot on the ground where the shadow is in my picture.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:38.760
Maybe Mr. Chewinski would like to help.

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:41.460
Excuse me, Mr. Chewinski, hi. Would you like to help?

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:44.460
Oh, he said yes!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:47.030
Here's where the shadow is now,

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:51.020
and here's where the shadow is in my picture.

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:53.520
When this part of the shadow gets to Mr. Chewinski,

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.910
it'll be about the same time as yesterday.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:57.920
Good job, Mr. Chewinski.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:00.000
I know. Thank you. Oh, you're welcome.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:04.440
Well, he didn't really do anything.

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:06.410
He did too!

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:11.520
So now we know that what Norman saw won't happen again until the shadow moves from there to

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.520
over there.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.780
So, what say you?

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:16.900
Let's go do naturey things!

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:17.890
Tally ho!

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:22.600
Onward and explore natureward!

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:19.060
Wait for the shadow to move just a little bit more.

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:26.220
Wait for it.

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:27.170
You're here.

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:28.140
Okay, good.

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:29.150
You ready?

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:30.000
Hooray!

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.480
something unbelievably, incredibly, amazingly, Nature Cat-y!

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:37.440
Whoa!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.730
The shadow!

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:42.570
It looks exactly like me!

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:43.570
That's unbelievable!

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:44.570
Incredible!

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:45.570
Amazing!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.750
Huh?

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:47.700
Told ya!

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:51.480
An everlasting memory!

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:53.010
Look!

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:54.010
The sun is moving!

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:55.840
And the shadows are changing!

00:21:55.840 --> 00:22:00.000
Thank you, Norman, for this splendid shadow!

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:06.160
surprise. Hey guys, what do you say we keep the shadow fun going? You wanna do hand shadows, Norman?

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:11.300
I am so down with that. Let's make more hand shadows.

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:20.460
Hey, what gives, man? Where's our shadows? No wonder. The sun is over there now.

00:22:20.460 --> 00:22:29.250
It's Ronald. My shadow's back! And it's big time!

00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:33.340
- Hello, Ronald.

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:35.780
- Oh, hello, Nature Cat.

00:22:35.780 --> 00:22:39.030
- Those are some pretty nifty hand shadows.

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:40.940
- Of course, Nature Cat.

00:22:40.940 --> 00:22:43.110
I'm the best.

00:22:43.110 --> 00:22:45.730
- So, the sun is on your side,

00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:49.610
so we can't make hand shadows on our side of the fence.

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:53.830
You mind if we join you on your side of the fence?

00:22:53.830 --> 00:22:56.420
- Well, okay, Nature Cat.

00:22:56.420 --> 00:22:59.120
But don't forget who the champion hand shadow maker is.

00:22:59.120 --> 00:22:59.730
Me!

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:04.370
Onward and let's make Hand Shadow's word!

00:23:04.370 --> 00:23:05.370
Woohoo!

00:23:05.370 --> 00:23:07.370
Woohoo!

00:23:07.370 --> 00:23:22.700
Nature Cat, Squeaks, Daisy, and Hal are cartoon characters and not real animals.

00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:27.200
To keep all of our animal friends safe, check with a grown up before you bring a pet on

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:29.830
your next nature adventure.
